<title>USA: CME OCT HOGS DOWN SHARPLY AS FUNDS SELL, CASH WEAK.</title>
<headline>CME OCT HOGS DOWN SHARPLY AS FUNDS SELL, CASH WEAK.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-08-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>CME October hog futures were sharply lower at mid-morning on fund selling and weakness in the cash market, floor sources said.</p>
<p>They noted R.J. O'Brien and LIT were featured sellers of October.</p>
<p>Cash hogs were $0.50 to $1.00 per cwt lower at key interior markets on Wednesday and expected to be steady to lower on Thursday.</p>
<p>At 1135 CDT Oct hogs were down 1.250 cent at 72.675 cents.</p>
<p>((-Chicago newsdesk 312-408 8720))</p>
